[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1656363848","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2053#issuecomment-1656363848","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2053","id":1656363848,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85iuhtI","user":{"login":"bsdimp","id":4139006,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzkwMDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4139006?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp","html_url":"https://github.com/bsdimp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-28T21:44:56Z","updated_at":"2023-07-28T21:44:56Z","body":"'All Rights Reserved' is part of the copyright notice, and not part of the license, per the Buenos Aires convention (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buenos_Aires_Convention). It was required on all copyright notices to preserve rights in certain Latin American countries from 1911 until the Berne convention was ratified obsoleting it in the year 2000. BSD has this phrase in it because the regents wanted to protect their rights in Central America. Since the first BSD licenses dated to the early 1980s (not ratified by the US until 1989, for example). We should move that phrase to the copyright notice given this historic detail. It has been removed from follow-on BSD projects like FreeBSD as well. See last bullet under Policy in https://www.freebsd.org/internal/software-license/ for example. If not already in that, we should make it optional text in the copyright notice.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1656363848/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1659159877","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2053#issuecomment-1659159877","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2053","id":1659159877,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85i5MVF","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-31T21:05:18Z","updated_at":"2023-07-31T21:05:18Z","body":"I think the one notable difference wrt BSD-3-Clause is that the disclaimer paragraph limitation of liability sentence adds \"patent infringement\" to the enumeration of things for which no liability is asserted.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1659159877/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1659411220","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2053#issuecomment-1659411220","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2053","id":1659411220,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85i6JsU","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-01T01:02:46Z","updated_at":"2023-08-01T01:02:46Z","body":"@richardfontana - I think you are correct. For reference here, in the \"including, but not limited to...\" parenthetical - this includes \"patent infringement\" whereas BSD-3-Clause does not. This begs the question of how operative a non-exhaustive list of examples is? Lawyers, thoughts? @coper